    "title": "Enterprise native recognized for competing in national Patriot Games - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ava Keel ,\n12 hours ago\nENTERPRISE, Ala. ( WDHN ) -- Enterprise Mayor William E. Cooper recognized a local high schooler for representing Alabama at the inaugural Freedom 250 Patriot Games 2026, a national competition celebrating America 250.\nDothan honors departing Fort Rucker commanding general as command exchanges hands Enterprise native Trevor Roen competed in the games as Alabama's Male Athlete Representative. Roen competed alongside high school athletes from around the country.\nPhotos courtesy of City of Enterprise Enterprise officials congratulated Roen for representing the City of Enterprise in the event, saying in a social media post :\n\"We are proud of Trevor for embracing this incredible opportunity and representing Enterprise and Alabama with such confidence and determination. Congratulations, Trevor!\"\nThe Patriot Games took place August 9-11 at SPIRE Academy in Geneva, Ohio.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WDHN - wdhn.com.\n1",
    "summary": "ENTERPRISE, Ala. ( WDHN ) -- Enterprise Mayor William E. Cooper recognized a local high schooler for representing Alabama at the inaugural Freedom 250 Patriot Games 2026, a national competition celebrating America 250. Dothan honors departing Fort Rucker commanding general as command exchanges hands Enterprise native Trevor Roen competed in the games as Alabama's Male Athlete Representative. Roen competed alongside high school athletes from around the country. The Patriot Games took place August 9-11 at SPIRE Academy in Geneva, Ohio. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WDHN - wdhn.com.",
